dtsls — install notes
=====================

Requirements
------------

* Linux (the server is Linux-only)
* A Rust toolchain: https://rustup.rs
* Optional, for binding validation:
    - a Linux kernel source tree, for
      Documentation/devicetree/bindings and include/dt-bindings
    - the dtschema python package: pip install dtschema
      (or point DTSLS_SCHEMAS_DIR at a package directory)

Build
-----

    cargo build --release

The binary lands at target/release/dtsls.

Install
-------

    install -Dm755 target/release/dtsls /usr/local/bin/dtsls

or, without root:

    install -Dm755 target/release/dtsls ~/.local/bin/dtsls

Make sure the install directory is on your PATH.

Verify
------

    dtsls --version

Cross-compiling (x86_64 from an aarch64 host, or vice versa)
------------------------------------------------------------

    rustup target add x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
    cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu

The binary lands at target/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/dtsls.

Neovim
------

    vim.lsp.config('dtsls', {
      cmd = { 'dtsls' },
      filetypes = { 'dts', 'dtsi', 'dtso', 'overlay' },
    })
    vim.lsp.enable('dtsls')

Open the editor's workspace at the kernel tree (or a board directory inside
it) so includes resolve and bindings are found. If your layout needs explicit
paths, pass initializationOptions:

    initializationOptions = {
      includePaths = { '/path/to/kernel/include' },
      bindingsPath = '/path/to/kernel/Documentation/devicetree/bindings',
    }

Logs and troubleshooting
------------------------

Logs go to $DTSLS_LOG (default /tmp/dtsls.log); verbosity via RUST_LOG
(e.g. RUST_LOG=debug). If binding validation or dt-bindings includes do not
resolve, the reason is reported as a diagnostic at the top of every file —
nothing degrades silently.

